# Core is protected. Changes under lib/core/** are the shared foundation every
# capture section depends on — a regression there breaks all five lines at once.
# See ARCHITECTURE.md §2.
#
# Features do NOT need to touch core. If a feature needs something from core,
# add it to core in its own reviewed commit, with tests.
#
# ── Why TWO owners, not one ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `main` requires an approving review from someone other than the last pusher.
# With a single code owner that combination deadlocks: the owner pushes a change
# to a protected path, CODEOWNERS demands an owner's review, and the only owner
# is the person who pushed. Nothing merges, and the workaround is to weaken the
# branch protection — which is worse than having no CODEOWNERS at all.
#
# Either owner satisfies the requirement, so listing both keeps the rule
# enforceable rather than theatrical. Add a third before removing either.

